1. Clone the GitHub repository:

   git clone https://github.com/nevzatolgun/NLOS_acoustic_identity_recognition.git

2. Open a terminal or Anaconda Prompt in the repository directory.

3. Create and activate a Python environment. Python 3.10 or 3.11 is
   recommended.

4. Install the core dependencies:

   pip install -r requirements.txt

5. Install PyTorch separately when the deep-learning baselines will be run.
   Select the PyTorch build appropriate for the available CPU, CUDA version,
   and GPU.

6. Set the acoustic data location.

   NLOS_AUDIO_ROOT must point to the directory recursively containing the
   authorized wall-reflection WAV files. The complete raw dataset is not
   included in the public repository.

   NLOS_OUTPUT_ROOT may optionally be set to a preferred output directory.
   Otherwise the publication package writes outputs under outputs/.

7. Spyder/F5 workflow

   Set code/ as the working directory, open the required run_*.py file, and
   press F5.

8. Command-line workflow

   cd code
   python run_classical_loso.py
   python run_synchronized_window_ablation.py
   python run_deep_learning_baselines.py
   python run_cross_material_analysis.py
   python run_human_empty_validation.py
